nnot  justify making a pasta carbonara on a  usual night it's basically just eggs  cheese bacon and a ton of carbs but when  you're using zucchini noodles mm-hmm I'm  like getting all the bacon so in a bowl  I'd beat together two eggs an egg yolk  and some Parmesan cheese and I set that  aside heat a large skillet over medium  heat and add one teaspoon of oil then  you add the pancetta cook it until crisp  and remove the bacon into a small dish  and return the pan to the stove add in  some more olive oil and bring the pan  back to a medium heat saute some minced  shallots for about two minutes then add  in some minced garlic for a minute next  add in the peas and stir until pretty  much thought through finally add in the  zucchini increase the heat to  medium-high and saute for just two to  three minutes or until fully warmed  through turn off the heat and toss the  zoodles with the egg cheese mixture for  no more than two minutes add in the  bacon and season with freshly cracked  black pepper top with some extra cheese  for good measure  and enjoy so guys I am so excited to dig  in so I'm going to get to that but what  I want you guys to do is to leave me a  comment below but your favorite comfort  foods are and that way I'm going to do a  little dish do-over with them in an  upcoming video so definitely leave me a  comment subscribe to the channel if you  like this video give me the thumbs up  and I'll see you next time on Abby's  kitchen
 

